---@field timeZone? string Optional. Specifies the time zone to be used in interpreting schedule. The value of this field must be a time zone name from the [tz database](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tz_database), like "America/New_York" or "UTC". Defaults to `UTC` if not specified.
---@field successCleanupRule? gcp.unstable.backupdr_v1beta.RestoreVerificationCleanupRule Optional. The cleanup rule to apply if the restore verification succeeds.
---@field failureCleanupRule? gcp.unstable.backupdr_v1beta.RestoreVerificationCleanupRule Optional. The cleanup rule to apply if the restore verification fails.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.backupdr_v1beta.StringMap Optional. User-defined labels.
---@field name? string Output only. Identifier. The resource name of the `RestoreVerificationPlan`. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/restoreVerificationPlans/{restoreVerificationPlan}`
---@field state? gcp.unstable.backupdr_v1beta.RestoreVerificationPlanStateEnum Output only. The `State` for the `RestoreVerificationPlan`.
---@field schedule? string Required. Describes the schedule on which the restore verification will be executed. The schedule is specified as a [Crontab](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron#Overview) string.
---@field createTime? string Output only. When the `RestoreVerificationPlan` was created.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the `RestoreVerificationPlan` resource. The description allows for additional details about `RestoreVerificationPlan` and its use cases to be provided. An example description is the following: "This is a restore verification plan that performs a daily verification and cleans up the resources immediately after." The description must be at most 2048 characters.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. When the `RestoreVerificationPlan` was last updated.

